; RED, stage 4: Ruined Chapel. Pews under pale silk, bell ropes twitching in still air.
; E minor hymn. Every bar opens with Sister Wren's signal from the belfry: three knocks,
; a pause. The bell (ring modulation) tolls at the end of each phrase, and the last bar
; lands on E major: the bell can still be rung.
;   sid1  three knocks, then the organ pedal
;   sid2  organ: broken chords
;   sid3  hymn melody and the bell
tempo 76
bars 16

inst knock wave=n,t arp=14,0,-5 adsr=0,5,0,2
inst pedal wave=p pw=45-55/0.2 adsr=3,0,12,8 filter=lp cut=500 res=0.3
inst organ wave=p pw=38-62/0.3 adsr=2,0,10,6
inst hymn  wave=s,p pw=30-45/0.3 vib=0.15 adsr=3,20,11,8 filter=lp cut=2600 res=0.2
inst bell  wave=t ring=2.76 adsr=0,50,0,40

$k: @knock v6 o3 e8
$p: @pedal v13 o2

; ---- sid1: knock knock knock, pause, pedal note
$1em: $k $k $k r8 $p e2 |
$1c:  $k $k $k r8 $p >c2< |
$1g:  $k $k $k r8 $p g2 |
$1b:  $k $k $k r8 $p b2 |
$1am: $k $k $k r8 $p a2 |
$1d:  $k $k $k r8 $p >d2< |

sid1: q8
sid1: $1em $1c $1g $1b $1em $1am $1b $1em
sid1: $1c $1d $1g $1em $1am $1b $1em $1em

; ---- sid2: organ eighths
$2em: o3 e b >e g b g e< b |
$2c:  o3 e >c e g >c< g e c< |
$2g:  o3 g >d g b >d< b g d< |
$2b:  o3 f# b >d# f# b f# d#< b |
$2am: o3 e a >c e a e c< a |
$2d:  o3 f# >d f# a >d< a f# d< |
$2e:  o3 e b >e g# b g# e< b |

sid2: @organ v7 l8 q8
sid2: $2em $2c $2g $2b $2em $2am $2b $2em
sid2: $2c $2d $2g $2em $2am $2b $2em $2e

; ---- sid3
$h: @hymn v10 o4
$l: @bell v7 o5

sid3: l4 q8
sid3: $h e2 g b | $h >c2 <b g | $h b2 >d <b | $h f#2 $l b2 |
sid3: $h e2 g b | $h >c2 e c< | $h b2 >d# <b | $h e2 $l >e2< |
sid3: $h >e2 d c< | $h >d2 c <a | $h b2 >d g< | $h >e2. r< |
sid3: $h >c2 <a >c< | $h b2 f# b | $h >e2 <b g | $h g#2 $l b2 |
